message.content:
Total ways to choose 3 cards from 52:

\[
\binom{52}{3}
\]

The deck has 26 red cards and 26 black cards.  
The only way the 3 cards are all the same color is if they are all red or all black:

\[
2\binom{26}{3}
\]

So the probability they are all the same color is

\[
\frac{2\binom{26}{3}}{\binom{52}{3}}
=
\frac{2 \cdot 2600}{22100}
=
\frac{5200}{22100}
=
\frac{4}{17}
\]

Therefore, the probability they are not all the same color is

\[
1-\frac{4}{17}
=
\frac{13}{17}
\]

The answer is \(\frac{13}{17}\).
